<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">Naranjo</h1><p class="st-meta">500 CE – 820 CE (approx.) · capital Naranjo</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Classic Maya kingdom in eastern Petén, called Sa'al, revived in the 7th century by Lady Six Sky, a princess from Dos Pilas.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Naranjo grew in the hills between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peten">Petén</a> lakes and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/belize">Belize</a> valley. Its dynasty claimed great antiquity, and by the 6th century, around 500 CE, its kings were regional powers, allied at times with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tikal">Tikal</a> and at others with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-kaan">Kingdom of Kaan</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aj-wosal-chan-kinich">Aj Wosal</a> Naranjo was a client of Kaan, but in the 620s and 630s <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/caracol">Caracol</a> defeated it. In 682 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lady-six-sky">Lady Six Sky</a> (Ix Wak Jalam Chan Ajaw), daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bajlaj-chan-kawiil">B'ajlaj Chan K'awiil</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/dos-pilas">Dos Pilas</a>, arrived to restore the dynasty. She acted as ruler for her young son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kahk-tiliw-chan-chaak">K'ahk' Tiliw Chan Chaak</a>, who fought wars against <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/yaxha">Yaxha</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ucanal">Ucanal</a> and other neighbours. Naranjo was also a centre of fine painted pottery.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Naranjo's last known monument dates to about 820, after which it declined in the Classic collapse. Heavy looting of its stelae in the 20th century prompted protection; it now lies within the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yaxha-nakum-naranjo-national-park">Yaxha-Nakum-Naranjo National Park</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/naranjo.jpg" alt="Naranjo" width="320" height="240"><figcaption>Image: Rudy Canales · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sitio_el_naranjo_1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>500 CE – 820 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>theocratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Naranjo</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Aj Wosal, Lady Six Sky, K'ahk' Tiliw Chan Chaak</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Maya religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Classic Maya</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Guatemala</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Sa'al, Saal</dd></dl></aside></div>

